* HIGH OUTPUT SENSITIVITY ONLY - UNRUN, NOT HARDWARE RATED
* VIN=50 V RL=17.8m; actual Iout is an unknown simulation result
* Source: sr_tank_dual_v33_ss_1ms_100a_phys.cir; only VIN and RL change.
* 100 A LOAD POINT (2026-10-31): identical to the round-4 1 ms deck except
* RL=18.9 mOhm, chosen for ~100 A at the fixed 24:1 ratio.  Model evidence
* only; no hardware.  Parent deck comments below still apply.
* CONVERGENCE CONTROL (round 3): same deck as sr_tank_dual_v33_ss_fine.cir but
* 1 ms long, saving 880..1000 us (24 SR periods) so a settling transient and a
* slow limit cycle can be told apart.  Everything else is identical.
* ============================================================================
* Step 3 joint bench: the REAL 48 V -> ~2 V resonant cavity with BOTH SRs of
* a rectifier pair replaced by the calibrated device model (SR_DEVICE) driven
* by the current timing model (sr_timing_v3_3, CGATE=0 CPIN=100p).
*
* STEADY-STATE-INIT VARIANT (2026-10-31 round 3).  Same power stage as v33,
* but SS is initialised at 4 V so the oscillator runs at its RT-only frequency
* (1/[2(6ns*1A/2.5615mA + 150ns)] = 200.6 kHz), not the 284.4 kHz soft-start point.
* THIS DECK: 1000 us, saved from 880 us (Tstart) -- see the .tran line; the
* paragraph below describes the parent deck sr_tank_dual_v33_ss_fine.cir.
* Parent deck: 500 us, saved from 440 us.  Differences from sr_tank_dual_v33.cir:
*   1. SS initialised at 4 V (200.6 kHz) instead of ramping from 0 (soft start).
*      VCC is ALSO held at 12 V from t=0.  .ic alone does NOT work with the
*      ramped VCC: while UVLO is unsatisfied FAULT is asserted, and the model's
*      SS discharge FET (RDIS=500) bleeds the 10 nF SS cap (tau = 5 us) for the
*      whole 2 us VCC ramp.  Measured: .ic V(ss)=4 + PWL VCC settles to 3.03 V
*      at 500 us -> 232.1 kHz, NOT the design point (probe _probe/ss_ic_b).
*      With VCC present from t=0 the fault window is ~30 ns, the same .ic is
*      preserved (V_SS 3.987 V at 20 us, 4.227 V at 500 us), and the oscillator
*      is at 200.6 kHz (probe _probe/ss_ic_a).  This deck is an
*      OPERATING-POINT initialisation, deliberately not a cold start; the
*      cold-start path is the unmodified sr_tank_dual_v33.cir.
*   2. FINE-TIMESTEP variant: 5 ns max step (the 30 ns run jittered period/Qrev by 1-5 %). Saves 440..500 us (Tstart=440u); it still runs 0..500 us.
*      LTspice REBASES the saved time axis to zero, so this deck's .meas below use
*      0..60 us, not the 440..500 us of the main deck.  Add 440 us to compare times.
*   3. MEASUREMENT TRAP: the SR gate period jitters +-1.3 % because turn-on is a
*      threshold event on the ringing drain; the PRIMARY period (V(sw)) is
*      200.59 kHz.  SR on-time alternates, so average over an EVEN number of
*      SR periods (this deck saves 12).
*   2. .save adds pair-1 device internals so tools/sr_energy_ledger.py can build
*      the branch energy ledger (channel, body diode, Cds/Cgd/Cgs, Ld/Ls/Lg, Rg).
* Gate-drive current I(xsr1:x1:bdrive) includes the 100 pF CPIN regularisation pad,
* so it is the total gate supply, not SR_DEVICE's gate pin alone.
*
* Derived from sim/v2/startup_ct.cir.  Power stage, transformer, resonant
* components, CT sense chain and UCC25600 behaviour are unchanged.  Only the
* four SR groups changed:
*   - ideal switch (SW Ron=1.5m) + ideal body diode + 2 nF node cap
*     -> Xsa/Xsb ... SR_DEVICE   (the 2 nF is dropped: SR_DEVICE carries Coss)
*   - sr_timing_v2 -> sr_timing_v3_3, CGATE=0 CPIN=100p (same as the g0
*     headline bench: the 6.7 nF surrogate is not used with a real device).
*     v3_3 = v3_2 + the turn-off comparator fix.  On this bench v3_2 latched
*     the first drain ring peak above OFFTH after the on-blank, so the gate
*     dropped after 525-1683 ns (mean 719 ns) where v2 and v3_3 hold 1455 ns;
*     the channel carried 5.2% of the SR energy (ech 0.571 uJ of ech+ebd
*     10.89 uJ) instead of 44.8% on v3_3, i.e. 4.7x the loss per device
*     (sr_tank_dual.raw, 1.5 ms run; sr_tank_dual_results.md section 4).
*     v3_2 = v3_1 + a soft rail on the off-blank integrator; without it this
*     deck never gets past t = 114.65 us (see the model header and
*     design/v2/sr_tank_dual_results.md).  The rail is 9.9-10 V, 15x above the
*     0.65 V decision level, so it does not change any timing result.
*   - PGD=0: the 0-ohm / fixed-10.9 V baseline the review asks to keep.
*
* WHY this bench exists (review step 3): the forced-sinusoid commutation bench
* imposes di/dt = 2*pi*f*I, so its "1.647 mV/A" VDS-peak slope is a property of
* that stimulus, not of a real tank.  Here the reverse current comes from real
* Lr/Cr energy exchange through the transformer leakage, so di/dt, reverse
* charge and the two channels' overlap current are measured on the tank.
*
* MEASUREMENT NOTES
*   Sign convention measured on sim/v2/startup_ct.raw (same power stage):
*   I(VSa1) < 0  rectifying (winding -> SR -> ground -> load -> winding),
*                and V(a1) = I*RdsOn < 0 as well
*   I(VSa1) > 0  reverse (current keeps flowing from ground back into the
*                winding while the channel is still on)
*   V(a1)  is the SR drain node; source is sgnd, so V(a1) is VDS.
*   ovl1 = min(max(-Ia,0), max(-Ib,0)): BOTH channels conducting FORWARD at the
*          same instant -- a current-based interlock check, not a gate-voltage
*          one (a wrong-signed probe here would measure reverse-current overlap,
*          which is normal commutation, not a shoot-through).  ovg1 is the
*          gate-voltage overlap kept only for contrast.
*   Charge/energy integrals are computed offline from the .raw over exactly one
*   switching period (tools/tank_metrics.py), so the window is explicit.
* RUN LENGTH AND INITIALISATION
*   The 1.5 ms deck (sr_tank_dual.cir) spends most of its run charging the 4 mF
*   output and is not settled when it stops.  This deck starts at the operating
*   point instead -- .ic V(out)=1.89 V(ss)=4 V, the real REG PWL kept because the pre-arm
*   window needs REG to pass through 0.1..4.1 V while VD>ARM (Bpl/Bpre in the
*   model; forcing REG=11 from t=0 latches the violation flag and every gate
*   stays off) -- and stops at 500 us, well after the output has settled.
*   This steady-state variant saves only 440-500 us (rebased to 0-60 us) and
*   its .meas windows are therefore 0-60 us; tools/tank_metrics.py averages the
*   last 8 periods of the saved window.
*
* Numerical result, not hardware validation.
* ============================================================================
.include ../../models/ucc25600_legacy_behaviour.lib
.include ../../models/sr_timing_v3_3.lib
.include ../../models/sr_device_v3.lib
.param PGD=0
.param VIN=50 RL=17.8m LP=10u LR_TOTAL=1u CR_TOTAL=620n
.param FS=1/(2*(6n/(2.5/976)+150n)) TS=1/FS DT=149n
Vbus vin0 0 {VIN}
Rin vin0 vin 1m
Cin vin 0 20u Rser=5m
Vaux aux 0 12
Xctl dt rt oc ss gd2 0 aux gd1 R184_UCC25600
Rdt dt 0 5.36k
Rrt rt 0 976
Css ss 0 10n
Rss_dc ss 0 1G
* ---- current transformer (unchanged from startup_ct.cir) -------------------
Lct1 nr nct 2u
Lct2 cs1 cs2 20m
Kct Lct1 Lct2 0.9999
D1 cs1 ocd DSCH
D2 cs2 ocd DSCH
D3 ocm cs1 DSCH
D4 ocm cs2 DSCH
.model DSCH D(Is=2n Rs=.3 N=1.2 Cjo=20p)
Vctg ocm 0 0
Rbur ocd ocm 10
Rf ocd oc1 1k
Cf oc1 ocm 47n
Rd1 oc1 oc 10k
Rd2 oc ocm 24k
Coc oc ocm 10n
* ---- primary side ----------------------------------------------------------
Dbt aux hb DBOOT
Cbt hb sw 220n Rser=.05
.model DBOOT D(Is=10n Rs=.5 N=1.2)
Bgh gh0 sw V=if(V(hb,sw)>5.5,if(delay(V(gd1),20n)>2,if(V(gd2)<2,V(hb,sw),0),0),0)
Bgl gl0 0 V=if(V(aux)>5.5,if(delay(V(gd2),20n)>2,if(V(gd1)<2,V(aux),0),0),0)
Rgh gh0 gh 3.2
Rgl gl0 gl 3.2
RgsH gh sw 10k
RgsL gl 0 10k
SH vin sw gh sw PRI_SW
DH sw vin BODY_P
Cgh gh sw 4n
Cdh vin sw 560p
SL sw 0 gl 0 PRI_SW
DL 0 sw BODY_P
Cgl gl 0 4n
Cdl sw 0 560p
.model PRI_SW SW(Ron=8m Roff=100Meg Vt=2.5 Vh=-.2)
.model BODY_P D(Ron=8m Roff=1G Vfwd=.7)
Cr sw nr {CR_TOTAL} Rser=3m
Lr nct p1 {LR_TOTAL} Rser=5m
Lp1 p1 p2 {LP} Rser=3m
Lp2 p2 p3 {LP} Rser=3m
Lp3 p3 p4 {LP} Rser=3m
Lp4 p4 0 {LP} Rser=3m
Lsa1 out a1 {LP/9} Rser=0.15m
Lsb1 b1 out {LP/9} Rser=0.15m
Lsa2 out a2 {LP/9} Rser=0.15m
Lsb2 b2 out {LP/9} Rser=0.15m
Lsa3 out a3 {LP/9} Rser=0.15m
Lsb3 b3 out {LP/9} Rser=0.15m
Lsa4 out a4 {LP/9} Rser=0.15m
Lsb4 b4 out {LP/9} Rser=0.15m
K1 Lp1 Lsa1 Lsb1 .999
K2 Lp2 Lsa2 Lsb2 .999
K3 Lp3 Lsa3 Lsb3 .999
K4 Lp4 Lsa4 Lsb4 .999
* ---- four rectifier groups, all real devices -------------------------------
Vreg reg sgnd PWL(0 0 130u 0 150u 11 1m 11)
VSa1 a1 da1 0
Xsa1 da1 ga1 sgnd SR_DEVICE
VSb1 b1 db1 0
Xsb1 db1 gb1 sgnd SR_DEVICE
Xsr1 a1 b1 ga1 gb1 reg sgnd pre1 SR_TIMING PGD={PGD} CGATE=0 CPIN=100p
VSa2 a2 da2 0
Xsa2 da2 ga2 sgnd SR_DEVICE
VSb2 b2 db2 0
Xsb2 db2 gb2 sgnd SR_DEVICE
Xsr2 a2 b2 ga2 gb2 reg sgnd pre2 SR_TIMING PGD={PGD} CGATE=0 CPIN=100p
VSa3 a3 da3 0
Xsa3 da3 ga3 sgnd SR_DEVICE
VSb3 b3 db3 0
Xsb3 db3 gb3 sgnd SR_DEVICE
Xsr3 a3 b3 ga3 gb3 reg sgnd pre3 SR_TIMING PGD={PGD} CGATE=0 CPIN=100p
VSa4 a4 da4 0
Xsa4 da4 ga4 sgnd SR_DEVICE
VSb4 b4 db4 0
Xsb4 db4 gb4 sgnd SR_DEVICE
Xsr4 a4 b4 ga4 gb4 reg sgnd pre4 SR_TIMING PGD={PGD} CGATE=0 CPIN=100p
Cout out sgnd 7.05m Rser=0.2m
Rload out sgnd {RL}
Vref sgnd 0 0
* ---- overlap probes --------------------------------------------------------
Bovl1 ovl1 0 V=min(max(-I(VSa1),0),max(-I(VSb1),0))
Bovg1 ovg1 0 V=if(V(ga1)>2,if(V(gb1)>2,1,0),0)
.options plotwinsize=0 method=gear
.tran 0 1000u 880u 5n uic
.ic V(out)=1.89 V(ss)=4
.save V(out) V(sw) V(reg) V(ss) I(Lr) V(a1) V(b1) V(ga1) V(gb1) I(VSa1) I(VSb1) I(Cin) I(Rin)
+ V(pre1) V(xsr1:q1) V(xsr1:q2) V(ovl1) V(ovg1) V(oc)
+ V(a4) V(b4) V(ga4) V(gb4) I(VSa4) I(VSb4) V(ovl4)
* ---- internal branch probes (pair 1 only): energy ledger ------------------
+ V(xsa1:di) V(xsa1:si) V(xsa1:gi) V(xsa1:gn) V(xsb1:di) V(xsb1:si) V(xsb1:gi) V(xsb1:gn)
+ I(xsa1:bch) I(xsa1:dbd) I(xsa1:cds) I(xsa1:cgd) I(xsa1:cgs) I(xsa1:rg) I(xsa1:lg) I(xsa1:ld) I(xsa1:ls)
+ I(xsb1:bch) I(xsb1:dbd) I(xsb1:cds) I(xsb1:cgd) I(xsb1:cgs) I(xsb1:rg) I(xsb1:lg) I(xsb1:ld) I(xsb1:ls)
+ I(xsr1:x1:bdrive) I(xsr1:x2:bdrive)
* ---- ledger probes (2026-11-01, issue #3): port + switch + CT + bias ----
+ I(Cout) I(SH) I(SL) I(DH) I(DL) I(Vaux) I(D1) I(D2) I(D3) I(D4) I(Rbur)
+ V(ocd) V(ocm) V(vin)
* CT burden needs its own node voltages: V(ocd) alone cannot price D1-D4.
+ V(cs1) V(cs2) V(nr) V(nct) I(Vreg)
.meas tran VOUT_AVG AVG V(out) FROM=0 TO=120u
.meas tran VOUT_RIP PP V(out) FROM=110u TO=120u
.meas tran VDS_A1_MIN MIN V(a1) FROM=0 TO=120u
.meas tran VDS_A1_MAX MAX V(a1) FROM=0 TO=120u
.meas tran IREV_A1 MAX I(VSa1) FROM=0 TO=120u
.meas tran IFWD_A1 MAX -I(VSa1) FROM=0 TO=120u
.meas tran OVL_CUR MAX V(ovl1) FROM=0 TO=120u
.meas tran OVL_GATE MAX V(ovg1) FROM=0 TO=120u
.meas tran IPRI_PK MAX abs(I(Lr)) FROM=0 TO=120u
.meas tran OUT_LAST FIND V(out) AT=120u
.end

